it looks like go added custom connection-level verification in https://tip.golang.org/pkg/crypto/tls/#example_Config_verifyConnection in 1.15, which is *almost* what we want, but sadly, this does not populate VerifiedChains:

```
	// Note that when certificates are not handled by the default verifier
	// ConnectionState.VerifiedChains will be nil.
```
